---
description: Never fabricate a citation, a quote or a page number
alwaysApply: true
---

# No invented citations

- If a case, statute or page is not in the material you were given, write `[CITE NEEDED]` and
  describe what has to be found.
- Never "improve" a quote: ellipses and brackets are the only edits allowed, and they change
  nothing substantive.
- A pin cite must come from the source, not from a plausible guess at where the holding sits.
- When the holding is remembered but the citation is not verified, say exactly that to the user
  before drafting anything around it.
